 :problem
 {:source "オーナー指示: \"kotobase の datomic 基盤の上に git, racile 相当を構築してね\"
           -- build a git-equivalent and Radicle-equivalent on top of
           kotobase's Datomic-shaped foundation"
  :facts
  ["A real Rust kotoba-git (byte-exact git object<->CID bridging, packfile
    decode, smart-HTTP v0) existed in kotoba-lang/kotoba and was deleted
    wholesale on 2026-07-01 (PR #259). ADR-2606251200's \"implemented and
    wired... proven end-to-end\" claim about it has no corresponding code
    anywhere in the repo as of this writing."
   "ADR-2607022600 (the CLJC migration roadmap rebuilding a Datomic-shaped
    substrate as prolly-tree/arrangement/chain/kotobase-peer/io-ipld/
    io-multiformats/org-ietf-cbor) explicitly excludes kotoba-git/kotoba-rad
    from its scope."
   "kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer (ADR-2607032430, ADR-2607032500: \"kotoba :
    kotobase = Clojure : Datomic\") is the real, actively-developed
    Datomic-shaped engine -- not real Datomic, not DataScript, a
    from-scratch 4-index (arrangement) + log-structured (chain) +
    content-addressed (prolly-tree/io-ipld) design, borrowing Datomic's
    vocabulary and API shape, not its code."
   "etzhayyim/root/70-tools/src/etzhayyim/kotoba_rad.cljc is a real,
    unit-tested RID/identity/sigref prototype, but uses its own hand-rolled
    raw-codec (0x55) CID implementation, independent of and incompatible
    with the io-multiformats/io-ipld scheme the actual kotobase-peer stack
    uses."]}

 :decision
 {:summary "Build kotoba-git (git-equivalent) and kotoba-rad
            (Radicle-equivalent) as two new, decoupled kotoba-lang CLJC
            repos, composed entirely from the existing kotobase-peer
            stack's real primitives, rather than reimplementing git's own
            SHA-1/packfile format or resurrecting the deleted Rust code."
  :layering
  ["kotoba-rad: RID/identity, delegate authorization, signed refs,
    push-gate -- built on chain + io-ipld + org-ietf-ed25519 (arrangement
    not required)"
   "kotoba-git: blob/tree/commit objects, ref store, DAG walk -- built on
    io-multiformats + org-ietf-cbor + io-ipld + arrangement"
   "kotobase-peer / arrangement / chain / prolly-tree / io-ipld: existing,
    unmodified"]
  :implementation
  ["kotoba-git.object: blobs are raw-codec (0x55) content-addressed bytes
    (multiformats.core/cidv1-raw); trees and commits are DAG-CBOR nodes
    (io-ipld, real CBOR tag-42 links, 0x71 codec). Commits carry a parents
    VECTOR -- a real commit DAG (merges representable), not a linear chain."
   "kotoba-git.refs: refs/heads/main-style mutable pointers as quads in an
    arrangement db, persisted via arrangement.core/commit! with identity
    blind/encrypt functions (refs are public repo metadata, no privacy
    semantics needed)."
   "kotoba-git.log: ancestors (full DAG reachability), log (first-parent
    history), missing-since (object-negotiation primitive for push/pull)."
   "kotoba-rad.identity: RID = CID of a repo's own genesis block
    ({did, created}) via io-ipld -- the SAME CID scheme kotoba-git uses for
    objects, unifying the two-CID-scheme fragmentation noted in :facts."
   "kotoba-rad.journal: append-only hash-chained log of identity events,
    built directly on kotoba-lang/chain -- chain's single-parent
    opaque-state design is exactly a linear identity journal, distinct from
    kotoba-git's N-parent commit DAG which chain's shape cannot represent."
   "kotoba-rad.delegate: folds journal into current authorized-delegate
    set; owner always authorized; every delegate-add/delegate-remove entry
    must carry a valid Ed25519 signature (org-ietf-ed25519) from an
    already-authorized did:key -- authority only flows forward from the
    genesis owner."
   "kotoba-rad.sigref + kotoba-rad.push-gate: signed ref->commit-cid
    attestations and authorize-push?, a pure-function reimplementation of
    the deleted Rust push_gate/RadRegistry, callable client- or
    server-side."
   "Two decoupled repos, not one: kotoba-rad only handles plain CID strings
    for refs/commits, never imports a kotoba-git object directly, so
    authorize-push? can gate any content-addressed system's ref updates."
   "Neither real Datomic, real git-CLI wire format, nor the deleted Rust
    code: consistent with kotobase-peer itself, arrangement/chain borrow
    Datomic's vocabulary not the product; kotoba-git borrows git's concepts
    (blob/tree/commit/refs/DAG history) via CID/DAG-CBOR content-addressing,
    not SHA-1/packfile -- no external consumer requires git-CLI byte
    compatibility."]
  :not-decided
  ["No git-CLI wire compatibility (no smart-HTTP bridge, no SHA-1 hashing,
    no binary packfile format); a distinct translation layer if ever
    needed, not attempted here."
   "No transport/replication wiring: kotoba-lang/p2p's deps.edn points at a
    renamed-away commit-dag coordinate and needs a patch first; its
    head-announce message has no signature field yet. Wiring
    authorize-push? into a signed head-announce is the natural next step,
    not attempted here."
   "No CACAO/SIWE delegation chains -- kotoba-rad.delegate uses direct
    Ed25519 did:key signing, not cacao.core/verify-chain-style root-first/
    leaf-last delegation. Deliberately deferred to keep the crypto surface
    small and directly testable."
   "No ref-policy (protected branches, fast-forward-only, etc) --
    authorize-push? checks who signed, not policy about what ref updates
    are allowed once authorized."
   "No restore-from-persisted-snapshot for kotoba-git.refs --
    arrangement.core/commit! is confirmed and used; a public
    'rehydrate a db from a snapshot CID' counterpart is not currently
    exposed by arrangement."]}

 :consequences
 ["etzhayyim/root/70-tools/src/etzhayyim/kotoba_rad.cljc's hand-rolled CID
   scheme is now a divergent, superseded prototype relative to
   kotoba-rad's io-ipld-based RID; migrating it (or the actor identity
   journals under etzhayyim/root/80-data/kotoba-rad/) onto this ADR's
   scheme is a follow-up, not done here."
  "Both new repos depend on the actively-churning kotobase-peer stack
   (three renames in the week before this ADR: quad-store+kqe->arrangement,
   commit-dag->chain, kotobase-engine->kotobase-peer). deps.edn pins exact
   :git/shas (not floating refs) for this reason; expect to re-verify
   upstream API shapes before extending either repo."
  "Neither repo is wired into any production surface (kotobase.net,
   kotobase.aozora.app) -- this ADR only establishes the primitives."]

 :verification
 ["kotoba-git: clojure -M:test -- 12 tests / 25 assertions, passing against
   both pinned :git/sha deps and local sibling checkouts
   (clojure -M:local:test). Covers blob/tree/commit round-trip, merge
   commits (multi-parent), tree entry ordering, DAG ancestor reachability,
   first-parent log, missing-since object negotiation, ref set/move/list/
   persist."
  "kotoba-rad: clojure -M:test -- 19 tests / 29 assertions, passing against
   both pinned :git/sha deps and local sibling checkouts. Covers RID
   genesis + content-addressing, journal append/read/hash-chain-tamper
   detection, delegate add/remove with real Ed25519 signature verification
   (including rejecting an unauthorized signer and honoring revocation),
   sigref sign/verify (including tamper detection), end-to-end
   authorize-push? (owner push, delegated push, outsider rejection,
   mismatched-target rejection, revoked-delegate rejection)."
  "No wrangler deploy / production wiring attempted for either repo."]}

 :addendum-2607072330-datom-native-object-model
 {:owner-instruction "「git は外部化するのではなく、kotoba-git で git 自体を
                       Datomic、kotoba で再設計実装してください」-- don't
                       externalize git as a side store; redesign git itself
                       on Datomic/kotoba, inside kotoba-git."
  :what-changed
  ["Original decision stored blob/tree/commit as io-ipld content-addressed
    DAG-CBOR blocks -- a store sitting NEXT TO arrangement (which only held
    refs). That is a git object store riding alongside the Datomic-shaped
    foundation, not git redesigned as part of it. Corrected."
   "kotoba-git.object's write-blob/write-tree/write-commit (trailing ! now
    dropped -- pure) assert blob/tree/commit content directly as
    arrangement quads whose SUBJECT is the object's own content hash:
    {cid \"blob/bytes\" bytes}, {cid \"tree/entries\" [...]}, {cid
    \"commit/tree\" (ipld/link tree)} + commit/parents/commit/author/
    commit/message/commit/ts. Every write fn is now (fn [db ...] -> [db'
    cid]), matching kotoba-git.refs's pre-existing db-in/db-out style, so
    object writes and ref updates thread the SAME db value."
   "io-multiformats/org-ietf-cbor/io-ipld now used ONLY for their pure
    canonical-encoding/hashing functions (cidv1-raw, encode+cid) to derive
    each object's content-addressed identity -- nothing persisted through
    them anymore. Persisting a repo to durable storage is one operation
    over the whole db (new kotoba-git.repo/persist!, wrapping
    arrangement.core/commit!), covering objects+refs together, the same
    path every other kotobase-peer domain uses."
   "Concrete Datomic-native payoff, not just a storage-location change:
    commit/tree asserted as a real ipld/link, so arrangement.core/refs-to
    answers 'which commits reference this tree' with zero extra code -- a
    reverse graph query the prior side-content-store design could not
    offer for free."
   "Trade-off accepted, stated plainly: commit/parents stored as one
    literal vector-of-links (not decomposed per-parent) to preserve parent
    order (first-parent history matters for log); cost is individual
    parents are not reverse-indexed via refs-to. ancestors/log/
    missing-since still walk the DAG procedurally, not as one Datalog
    query -- arrangement.datalog is conjunctive-join only, not (yet)
    transitive-closure/fixpoint (ADR-2607022600 already flags this as an
    open follow-up for the whole stack, not resolved here)."
   "kotoba-rad untouched: it never depended on kotoba-git's object
    representation (only plain CID strings) -- the decoupling from the
    original decision paid off exactly as intended when this half of the
    design changed underneath it."]
  :verification
  ["kotoba-git suite grew 12->14 tests / 25->28 assertions (added
    kotoba-git.repo-test + an arrangement.core/refs-to reverse-lookup
    test), all green against both pinned :git/sha deps and local sibling
    checkouts."
   "Full cross-repo integration script from this ADR's original
    Verification section (RID -> delegate -> object write -> sigref ->
    authorize-push? -> ref move -> second commit -> revoke ->
    outsider-rejection) re-run end-to-end against the new API, identical
    pass/fail results, plus a new step showing arrangement.core/refs-to
    resolving tree-2's referencing commit with no kotoba-git-specific
    code."]}

 :addendum-2607072400-ref-policy-signed-announce-cacao
 {:summary "Three follow-on iterations (driven by the owner's recurring
            \"成熟度, coverageを向上\" direction) closed gaps this ADR's
            original :not-decided section named."
  :ref-policy
  ["New kotoba-git.ref-policy: fast-forward? (old target nil, equal, or
    an ancestor of the new one via kotoba-git.log/ancestors) and
    set-ref-ff-only! (throws, ref untouched, on a non-fast-forward).
    Shape policy, composable with but independent of kotoba-rad's
    identity policy -- no single function combines both yet. 23->32
    tests / 51->68 assertions."]
  :signed-head-announce
  ["kotoba-lang/p2p: optional new-node 3-arity opts map
    (:sign-announce/:verify-announce?, both default no-op, existing
    2-arity callers unaffected) -- PR #1, merged after CI (JVM + real
    ClojureScript) passed. Closes that namespace's own docstring note
    that head-record signing was 'a tracked follow-up'. 9 tests / 19
    assertions (5 new)."
   "New kotoba-rad.announce: a p2p head-announce ({:graph :head-cid :seq})
    is exactly a sigref shape (ref-name=graph, commit=head-cid, ts=seq),
    so no new signing primitive was needed, only this adapter. kotoba-rad
    34->40 tests / 55->62 assertions."
   "Corrected a standing inaccuracy in both READMEs claiming p2p's
    deps.edn needed a commit-dag->chain patch -- already fixed upstream,
    independently, before this was checked."]
  :cacao-delegation-chains
  ["New kotoba-rad.cacao-delegate + push-gate/authorize-push-cacao? (new
    dependency org-chainagnostic-cacao): a second, journal-free
    authorization scheme alongside kotoba-rad.delegate's ledger -- owner
    mints a CACAO (CAIP-122/SIWE) capability chain (root-first, leaf-last,
    cacao.core/verify-chain) granting a push-resource string to a
    delegate's did:key; the delegate presents that chain (or a further
    sub-delegated link) to prove authorization with no journal lookup."
   "Verified: single-link exact/wildcard grants, two-link sub-delegation
    to a third party, sub-delegation cannot escalate resources beyond
    what the delegator holds (cacao.core's own covers? constraint), wrong
    root issuer / wrong claimed holder rejected, expiry enforced when
    checked. 40->50 tests / 62->76 assertions."
   "Known gap, documented rather than solved: no revocation without an
    expiry (unlike the journal's remove-delegate!)."]}

 :addendum-2607072500-cross-repo-verification-found-a-real-bug
 {:summary "A /verify-style pass loaded kotoba-git + kotoba-rad +
            kotoba-lang/p2p together in one process (a real downstream
            consumer's classpath) rather than trusting each repo's own
            isolated test suite. set-ref-guarded! and the CACAO
            delegation chain verified cleanly this way; the signed
            head-announce integration did not."
  :finding
  ["kotoba-lang/p2p's chain pin predated ADR-2607050800's internal
    commit-dag->chain rename (still required commit-dag.core). Looked
    harmless in every isolated check this session ran on p2p alone -- its
    own test suite pinned the same stale SHA consistently, nothing ever
    contradicted it."
   "The moment a real consumer also depended on chain at a CURRENT SHA
    (kotoba-rad does), tools.deps resolved one version for the whole
    classpath, and picking the newer one broke p2p's own commit-dag.core
    require -- confirmed directly: (require 'chain.core) failed,
    (require 'commit-dag.core) succeeded, on the merged classpath (the
    reverse held before the fix)."
   "Silently blocked the exact integration kotoba-rad.announce +
    kotoba-lang/p2p's hooks were built for -- no amount of testing either
    repo in isolation could have caught it."]
  :fix
  ["kotoba-lang/p2p PR #2, merged after CI green on both JVM and real
    ClojureScript: pinned chain to the same SHA kotoba-rad uses; changed
    the require from commit-dag.core to chain.core (API unchanged by the
    rename -- pure coordinate/require update)."]
  :verification
  ["Re-verified after the fix, end-to-end, for real (not the
    contract-level workaround the initial verification pass had to fall
    back to): a delegate signed a real 2-node chain.core commit history
    via kotoba-rad.announce's hooks; the receiving node fully converged
    (bitswap/hydrate genuinely ran, not just message-passing) to the
    signed head; the same receiver correctly REJECTED a real, valid,
    further-ahead but UNSIGNED announce from the same peer, leaving its
    head unchanged."
   "kotoba-rad: docs-only update recording the now-verified integration.
    p2p: 9 tests / 19 assertions, unchanged count, green on the corrected
    pin."]
  :lesson
  "Generalizes past this one bug: this session's per-repo test suites
   (and even the first cross-repo /verify pass's unit-level checks) were
   each internally consistent and each green, and none of that surfaced
   the conflict -- only actually loading the repos a real consumer would
   combine, together, in one process, did."}}
